[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4522389606","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119670#issuecomment-4522389606","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119670","id":4522389606,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDY4wZg","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-22T20:07:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T20:07:21Z","body":"Can't it be unified with the ERR macro, like `ANIM_ERR_NULL()`?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4522389606/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4522665127","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119670#issuecomment-4522665127","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119670","id":4522665127,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDZJkpw","user":{"login":"Ryan-000","id":73148864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTQ4ODY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73148864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000","html_url":"https://github.com/Ryan-000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-22T21:00:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T21:00:43Z","body":"> Can't it be unified with the ERR macro, like `ANIM_ERR_NULL()`?\r\n\r\nI don't think so. \r\n\r\nThe issue descriptor's have to be declared somewhere for deduplication reasons, so we don't show warnings and errors for the same issue ID (e.g. for animation_not_set, missing_input_connection).\r\n\r\nThere is too much variety as well.\r\n- Some issues are warnings during `prepare`, while others are errors. \r\n- Some require the input index.\r\n- Some require message formatting arguments. \r\n- During prepare, they are added to the `AnimationTree`, but during `_process` they are added to `ProcessState`\r\n\r\nThe only scenario right now, in which I can see a benefit would be in `AnimationNodeBlendSpace*D`, but TBH that should probably be changed to be a warning during `prepare`, and an error at `_process` like the others.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4522665127/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4522718225","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119670#issuecomment-4522718225","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119670","id":4522718225,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDZM0EQ","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-22T21:11:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T21:17:31Z","body":"So how about `AnimationTree::push_issue(bool p_is_error, IssueType p_type, vararg Variant)` then `p_tree.push_issue(is_error, ISSUE_TYPE_ANY, instance, node, anymore)` ?\r\nOr `AnimationTree::push_issue(bool p_is_error, ExtendedIssue p_issue)` then `p_tree.push_issue(is_error, ExtendedIssue(instance, \"NodeName\", \"AndMore\"))` ?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4522718225/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4523199679","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119670#issuecomment-4523199679","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119670","id":4523199679,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDZqMvw","user":{"login":"Ryan-000","id":73148864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTQ4ODY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73148864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000","html_url":"https://github.com/Ryan-000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-22T22:52:30Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T22:52:30Z","body":"> So how about `AnimationTree::push_issue(bool p_is_error, IssueType p_type, vararg Variant)` then `p_tree.push_issue(is_error, ISSUE_TYPE_ANY, instance, node, anymore)` ? Or `AnimationTree::push_issue(bool p_is_error, ExtendedIssue p_issue)` then `p_tree.push_issue(is_error, ExtendedIssue(instance, \"NodeName\", \"AndMore\"))` ?\r\n\r\nThe proposed API seems less strongly typed to me (`bool p_is_error` and `vararg Variant`), so I am not sure what advantage it has over the current builder approach.\r\n\r\nIs the goal to reduce call-site verbosity, change how issues are defined, or something else?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4523199679/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4523215818","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119670#issuecomment-4523215818","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119670","id":4523215818,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDZrLyg","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-22T22:57:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T23:11:26Z","body":"It is a matter of maintainability and readability. This is because it is difficult for anyone other than you to guess what should be input for error output using method chaining. If they were argument names, other people would also know what to input.\r\n\r\nAFAIK, there are no other places besides the well-documented Tween that use the builder pattern. If there are no other classes that use the builder pattern to output messages, I believe that there is no possibility of implementing the builder pattern specifically here.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4523215818/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4523317586","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119670#issuecomment-4523317586","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119670","id":4523317586,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDZxZUg","user":{"login":"Ryan-000","id":73148864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTQ4ODY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73148864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000","html_url":"https://github.com/Ryan-000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-22T23:22:20Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T23:22:20Z","body":"> It is a matter of maintainability and readability. This is because it is difficult for anyone other than you to guess what should be input for error output using method chaining. If they were argument names, other people would also know what to input.\r\n> \r\n> AFAIK, there are no other places besides the well-documented Tween that use the builder pattern. If there are no other classes that use the builder pattern to output messages, I believe that there is no possibility of implementing the builder pattern specifically here.\r\n\r\nI can remove the fluent builder and replace it with methods like:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid AnimationTree::push_issue(\r\n\t\tconst AnimationNode::Issue::Descriptor &p_descriptor,\r\n\t\tAnimationNode::Issue::Severity p_severity,\r\n\t\tconst StringName &p_path,\r\n\t\tint p_input_index = -1,\r\n\t\tconst Array &p_message_arguments = Array());\r\n\r\nvoid AnimationNode::ProcessState::push_error(\r\n\t\tconst AnimationNode::Issue::Descriptor &p_descriptor,\r\n\t\tconst StringName &p_path,\r\n\t\tint p_input_index = -1,\r\n\t\tconst Array &p_message_arguments = Array());\r\n```\r\n\r\nI would still keep `Descriptor` and `Issue::Severity`, to avoid a parallel `IssueType` message table and to keep severity extensible if informational diagnostics are added later.\r\n\r\nIf needed, the `p_input_index` can be moved into the formatting arguments, though the internals would be a bit more complicated.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4523317586/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4523439403","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119670#issuecomment-4523439403","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119670","id":4523439403,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDZ41Kw","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-23T00:03:32Z","updated_at":"2026-05-23T00:04:21Z","body":"To be honest, I am skeptical about whether it is necessary to add such a complex structure just to push errors and warnings. I believe that it is necessary to output errors during the actual blending, but I do not think warnings will be needed at runtime.\r\n\r\nWould it not be sufficient to just have functions like `tree.push_error_null()` or `tree.push_error_msg()` during blending, and functions like `tree.push_warning_null()` or `tree.push_warning_msg()` when traversing the tree after changes in the editor (means it should be in the `#ifdef TOOLS_ENABLED` block)?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4523439403/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4526919473","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119670#issuecomment-4526919473","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119670","id":4526919473,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDdNPMQ","user":{"login":"Ryan-000","id":73148864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTQ4ODY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73148864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000","html_url":"https://github.com/Ryan-000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-24T00:28:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-24T00:28:12Z","body":"I made some changes to simplify it. \r\n\r\nNow any issues during prepare are warnings, while issues pushed during process (the active blend path) are \"errors\".\r\n\r\nI ended up removing `ProcessState::valid` since it seems all issues are non-fatal, so the tree can just do its best to animate.\r\n\r\nBut if stopping the entire tree is still desired, I can add it back.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4526919473/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]